<title>ARGENTINA: TABLE - ARGENTINA POSTS $129 MLN TRADE GAP IN JUNE.</title>
<headline>TABLE - ARGENTINA POSTS $129 MLN TRADE GAP IN JUNE.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a breakdown of Argentine foreign trade data released by the Economy Ministry Wednesday:</p>
<p>			   1997		   1996</p>
<p>June</p>
<p>    Exports	    2,212		  2,206</p>
<p>    Imports	    2,341		  1,996</p>
<p>    Balance	    (129)		    210</p>
<p>Six months</p>
<p>    Exports	   12,565		 11,344</p>
<p>    Imports	   13,837		 10,711</p>
<p>    Balance	   (1,272)		   633</p>
<p>Note: In millions of dollars.  </p>
<p>Exports to Mercosur partners Brazil, Uruguay and Paraguay in the first half were $4.21 billion, up 18 percent from the 1996 period. Imports from them were $3.31 billion, up 27 percent from the first six months of 1996.</p>
<p>Argentina exported $2.08 billion to the European Union, down 14 percent, while imports rose 32 percent to $4.05 billion.</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires newsroom, 541 318-0618))</p>
